  "Question": "$X$ follows $B(2,1/2)$. What is $P(X=1)$?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "1/2",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "$C(2,1)\\times1/4=1/2$.\n\nAlternative method 1: Enumerate the outcomes\n\nLet \\(S\\) mean success and \\(F\\) mean failure. Each has probability \\(1/2\\). The two independent trials give exactly four sequences, \\(SS,SF,FS,FF\\), each with probability \\((1/2)^2=1/4\\). The list covers both possibilities for each trial once. Exactly one success occurs in \\(SF\\) or \\(FS\\), so\n\\[\nP(X=1)=\\frac{2}{4}=\\frac12.\n\\]",
